IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sga-time`
IMPORT `sga-part2`
IMPORT `sga-part3a`
IMPORT `sga-part3b`
IMPORT `sga-choice-of-fund`
IMPORT `sga-part4-6`
IMPORT `sga-part7`
IMPORT `sga-parts8-9`

-- Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Commonwealth), sections 1 to 80,
-- Federal Register compilation C2026C00272 (Compilation No. 78, from 1 July 2026), plain-text conversion (not the authorised text).
-- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an employer, or an adviser to one, asking whether superannuation guarantee charge is payable,
-- how the individual and the base shortfalls are worked out, what the choice of fund requirements need,
-- when a statement or payment is due, and what penalty follows late payment.
--
-- Every question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the employer can state, each with an @desc worded as the employer would be asked.
-- The records and lists the layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers,
-- and the SAME layer-1 rule is then called: no rule is restated here and no layer-1 module changes to suit this layer.
-- Provisions that address only the Commissioner appear here only for what they mean to the employer.
-- The questions follow the order of the text: Part 2 (who is an employee), Part 3 (the amount, the shortfall and the charge),
-- Part 3A (choice of fund), Part 4 (statements and assessments), Part 6 (unpaid charge), Part 7 (the notice to pay and the penalty),
-- Part 8 (payments to employees), Part 9 (the amnesty and records).
-- Whole-quarter questions take the QE day as a plain date, as the layer-1 time module does.

§ `Part 2: who is my employee`

-- s 12. Subject to the section, "employee" and "employer" have their ordinary meaning; subsections (2) to (11) expand it or make particular provision.
@export Must I treat this person as my employee for superannuation guarantee (s 12)?
GIVEN `the person is an employee in the ordinary meaning of the word` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person your employee in the ordinary meaning of the word?
      `the person is entitled to payment for duties as a member of the executive body of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person entitled to be paid for duties as a member of the executive body of a body corporate?
      `the person works under a contract wholly or principally for their labour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person work under a contract that is wholly or principally for the person's labour?
      `the person is a member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth or of a State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth or of a State?
      `the person is a member of the Legislative Assembly of the ACT or the NT` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the Legislative Assembly of the Australian Capital Territory or of the Northern Territory?
      `the person is paid to perform in an entertainment or sport, or in connection with a film, tape, disc or broadcast` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person paid to perform or present, or to provide services in connection with, an entertainment, sport or similar activity, or a film, tape, disc or broadcast?
      `the person holds an office or position under a law, or is otherwise in the service of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold or perform the duties of an appointment, office or position under the Constitution or a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, or is the person otherwise in the service of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory?
      `the person holds office as a member of a local government council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold office as a member of a local government council?
      `the person is covered by paragraph 12-45(1)(e) in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person covered by paragraph 12-45(1)(e) in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953?
      `the person is paid to do domestic work for not more than 30 hours per week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person paid to do work wholly or principally of a domestic or private nature for not more than 30 hours per week?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I treat this person as my employee` MEANS
    `is an employee for the purposes of the Act` mine
    WHERE
        mine MEANS Engagement OF
                                `the person is an employee in the ordinary meaning of the word`,
                                `the person is entitled to payment for duties as a member of the executive body of a body corporate`,
                                `the person works under a contract wholly or principally for their labour`,
                                `the person is a member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth or of a State`,
                                `the person is a member of the Legislative Assembly of the ACT or the NT`,
                                `the person is paid to perform in an entertainment or sport, or in connection with a film, tape, disc or broadcast`,
                                `the person holds an office or position under a law, or is otherwise in the service of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`,
                                `the person holds office as a member of a local government council`,
                                `the person is covered by paragraph 12-45(1)(e) in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953`,
                                `the person is paid to do domestic work for not more than 30 hours per week`

§ `Part 3: the amount I must contribute (ss 10A, 15A to 17D)`

-- s 10A(6). The maximum contributions base is worked out from the concessional contributions cap and the charge percentage.
@export What is the maximum contributions base for the year (s 10A(6))?
GIVEN `the concessional contributions cap for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the concessional contributions cap for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the maximum contributions base for the year` MEANS
    `the maximum contributions base` `the concessional contributions cap for the year` `the charge percentage`

-- s 10A. A payment of qualifying earnings counts only up to the base for the year.
@export How much of a payment I make counts as qualifying earnings (s 10A)?
GIVEN `the total I have already paid this employee in qualifying earnings during the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much qualifying earnings have you already paid this employee during the financial year, in dollars?
      `the payment I am making` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are you paying now, in dollars?
      `the maximum contributions base for the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum contributions base for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my payment counts as qualifying earnings` MEANS
    `the amount of the payment that is treated as qualifying earnings`
        `the total I have already paid this employee in qualifying earnings during the financial year`
        `the payment I am making`
        `the maximum contributions base for the year I am asking about`

-- ss 15A, 15C, 17A. The individual superannuation guarantee amount for an employee and a QE day is the charge percentage of the qualifying earnings on the QE day, nil if a shortfall exemption certificate is in force.
@export What is my individual superannuation guarantee amount for an employee for the QE day (ss 15A, 15C, 17A)?
GIVEN `the qualifying earnings I paid this employee earlier in the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much qualifying earnings had you paid this employee earlier in the financial year, before this QE day, in dollars?
      `the maximum contributions base for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum contributions base for the year, in dollars?
      `the payments of qualifying earnings I made to this employee for the QE day` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What payments of qualifying earnings did you make to this employee for the QE day, in dollars, one after another?
      `a shortfall exemption certificate is in force for this employee and a period that includes the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an employer shortfall exemption certificate in force for this employee and a period that includes the QE day?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my individual superannuation guarantee amount` MEANS
    `the individual superannuation guarantee amount`
        `the qualifying earnings I paid this employee earlier in the financial year`
        `the maximum contributions base for the year`
        `the payments of qualifying earnings I made to this employee for the QE day`
        `a shortfall exemption certificate is in force for this employee and a period that includes the QE day`

-- s 17C(4)(c), s 17D. Does the period specified in my employer shortfall exemption certificate include the QE day?
@export Does my employer shortfall exemption certificate cover the QE day (s 17D)?
GIVEN `the first day of the period specified in the certificate` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period specified in the certificate?
      `the last day of the period specified in the certificate` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period specified in the certificate?
      `the QE day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the QE day you are asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does my certificate cover the QE day` MEANS
    `the period specified in the certificate includes the QE day`
        `the first day of the period specified in the certificate`
        `the last day of the period specified in the certificate`
        `the QE day I am asking about`

§ `Part 3: which contributions count, and the base shortfall (ss 18A to 18C)`

-- s 18A(1), 18A(2), 18A(3), 18B. Does this contribution I made count as an eligible contribution?
@export Does a contribution I made count as an eligible contribution (ss 18A, 18B)?
GIVEN `it is a sacrificed contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a contribution the employee sacrificed from salary or wages?
      `it is to a complying superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a contribution to a complying superannuation fund?
      `it is able to be allocated within the fund for the benefit of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it able to be allocated within the fund for the benefit of the employee?
      `it is for the employee as a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made for the employee as a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme?
      `a conversion notice has effect in relation to the fund when it is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a conversion notice have effect in relation to the fund at the time you make it?
      `it is to a retirement savings account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a contribution to a retirement savings account?
      `it is able to be allocated within the retirement savings account for the benefit of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it able to be allocated within the retirement savings account for the benefit of the employee?
      `the employee has died and I pay the equivalent to the legal personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the employee died, and are you paying the equivalent of the contribution to the employee's legal personal representative?
      `it is notionally made to a defined benefit scheme for the employee as a defined benefit member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it notionally made to a defined benefit superannuation scheme for the employee as a defined benefit member of the scheme?
      `I have a written statement by or for the trustee that the fund is a resident regulated superannuation fund and is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before or when you made it, did you obtain a written statement by or for the trustee that the fund is a resident regulated superannuation fund not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993?
      `section 18B(2) applies on the day I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 18B(2) apply on the day you made it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` MEANS
    `is an eligible contribution` mine
    WHERE
        mine MEANS `Contribution made for the benefit of an employee` OF
                                `it is a sacrificed contribution`,
                                `it is to a complying superannuation fund`,
                                `it is able to be allocated within the fund for the benefit of the employee`,
                                `it is for the employee as a defined benefit member of a defined benefit superannuation scheme`,
                                `a conversion notice has effect in relation to the fund when it is made`,
                                `it is to a retirement savings account`,
                                `it is able to be allocated within the retirement savings account for the benefit of the employee`,
                                `the employee has died and I pay the equivalent to the legal personal representative`,
                                `it is notionally made to a defined benefit scheme for the employee as a defined benefit member`,
                                `I have a written statement by or for the trustee that the fund is a resident regulated superannuation fund and is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993`,
                                `section 18B(2) applies on the day I made it`

-- s 18C(1)(c), 18C(2). The latest day a contribution can be received and still be applied for the QE day: the usual period, or the latest day under the table of allowable longer periods.
@export By what day must a contribution be received by the fund to count for the QE day (s 18C)?
GIVEN `the QE day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the QE day you are asking about?
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days between the QE day and the end of the usual period are public holidays?
      `item 1 of the table in section 18C(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does item 1 of the table in section 18C(2) apply to you?
      `the first standard QE day after the QE day I am asking about` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If item 2 of the table applies, what is the first standard QE day after the QE day you are asking about?
      `the day a determination covering me and the QE day was made` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If item 3 of the table applies, on what day was the determination covering you and the QE day made?
      `the latest due day` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If item 4 of the table applies, what is the latest due day?
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must a contribution be received to count` MEANS
    `the latest day an eligible contribution is able to be applied for the QE day`
        `the QE day I am asking about`
        `the public holidays`
        (`the latest day under the table of allowable longer periods`
            `the QE day I am asking about`
            `the public holidays`
            `item 1 of the table in section 18C(2) applies`
            `the first standard QE day after the QE day I am asking about`
            `the day a determination covering me and the QE day was made`
            `the latest due day`)

-- s 18C(1)(c). Was this contribution received in time to count for the QE day?
@export Was a contribution received by the fund in time to count for the QE day (s 18C)?
GIVEN `the QE day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the QE day you are asking about?
      `the day the fund received the contribution` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the fund, RSA or scheme receive the contribution?
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days between the QE day and the end of the usual period are public holidays?
      `item 1 of the table in section 18C(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does item 1 of the table in section 18C(2) apply to you?
      `the first standard QE day after the QE day I am asking about` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If item 2 of the table applies, what is the first standard QE day after the QE day you are asking about?
      `the day a determination covering me and the QE day was made` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If item 3 of the table applies, on what day was the determination covering you and the QE day made?
      `the latest due day` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If item 4 of the table applies, what is the latest due day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was my contribution received in time to count` MEANS
    `a day of receipt is within the periods for the QE day`
        `the QE day I am asking about`
        `the day the fund received the contribution`
        `the public holidays`
        (`the latest day under the table of allowable longer periods`
            `the QE day I am asking about`
            `the public holidays`
            `item 1 of the table in section 18C(2) applies`
            `the first standard QE day after the QE day I am asking about`
            `the day a determination covering me and the QE day was made`
            `the latest due day`)

-- A helper for the questions that follow: it pairs the amounts the employer gives with the days the fund received them, one for one.
GIVEN amounts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      days IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Eligible contribution received`
`the contributions received, pairing each amount with its day` MEANS
    CONSIDER amounts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY moreAmounts THEN
        CONSIDER days
        WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
        WHEN d FOLLOWED BY moreDays THEN
            (`Eligible contribution received` OF a, d) FOLLOWED BY (`the contributions received, pairing each amount with its day` moreAmounts moreDays)

-- s 18C(1). The individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall: the individual superannuation guarantee amount less the eligible contributions relevant for the QE day.
@export What is the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall for an employee (s 18C)?
GIVEN `the individual superannuation guarantee amount for this employee and the QE day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the individual superannuation guarantee amount for this employee and the QE day, in dollars?
      `the QE day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the QE day you are asking about?
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days between the QE day and the end of the usual period are public holidays?
      `item 1 of the table in section 18C(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does item 1 of the table in section 18C(2) apply to you?
      `the first standard QE day after the QE day I am asking about` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If item 2 of the table applies, what is the first standard QE day after the QE day you are asking about?
      `the day a determination covering me and the QE day was made` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If item 3 of the table applies, on what day was the determination covering you and the QE day made?
      `the latest due day` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If item 4 of the table applies, what is the latest due day?
      `the amounts of my eligible contributions for this employee, in the order the fund received them` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What amounts of eligible contributions did you make for this employee, in dollars, in the order the fund received them?
      `the days the fund received them` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On what days did the fund, RSA or scheme receive those contributions, in the same order?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my individual base shortfall` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the total of the eligible contributions received in the periods for the QE day`
                 `the QE day I am asking about`
                 `the public holidays`
                 (`the latest day under the table of allowable longer periods`
                     `the QE day I am asking about`
                     `the public holidays`
                     `item 1 of the table in section 18C(2) applies`
                     `the first standard QE day after the QE day I am asking about`
                     `the day a determination covering me and the QE day was made`
                     `the latest due day`)
                 (`the contributions received, pairing each amount with its day`
                     `the amounts of my eligible contributions for this employee, in the order the fund received them`
                     `the days the fund received them`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST total THEN JUST (`the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall` `the individual superannuation guarantee amount for this employee and the QE day` total)

§ `Part 3: the final shortfall, notional earnings and the uplift (ss 18D, 19A, 19B)`

-- s 18D, s 19A(1). How many days the late period has: from the day after the latest day a contribution could be applied to the day the assessment is made.
@export How many days are in the late period for the QE day (ss 18D, 19A)?
GIVEN `the latest day a contribution could be applied for the QE day` IS A DATE @desc What was the latest day an eligible contribution was able to be applied for the QE day?
      `the day the assessment is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the assessment made?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days are in my late period` MEANS
    `the number of days in the late period` `the latest day a contribution could be applied for the QE day` `the day the assessment is made`

-- s 18D. The individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall: the base shortfall less the eligible contributions received during the late period.
@export What is the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall for an employee (s 18D)?
GIVEN `the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall for this employee and the QE day, in dollars?
      `the latest day a contribution could be applied for the QE day` IS A DATE @desc What was the latest day an eligible contribution was able to be applied for the QE day?
      `the day the assessment is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the assessment made?
      `the amounts of my eligible contributions for this employee, in the order the fund received them` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What amounts of eligible contributions did you make for this employee that were not applied for an earlier QE day, in dollars, in the order the fund received them?
      `the days the fund received them` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On what days did the fund, RSA or scheme receive those contributions, in the same order?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my individual final shortfall` MEANS
    `the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall`
        `the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall`
        (`the total of the eligible contributions received during the late period`
            `the latest day a contribution could be applied for the QE day`
            `the day the assessment is made`
            (`the contributions received, pairing each amount with its day`
                `the amounts of my eligible contributions for this employee, in the order the fund received them`
                `the days the fund received them`))

-- s 19A. The individual notional earnings component: the general interest charge, compounded daily, on the base shortfall; nil if the final shortfall is nil.
@export What is the individual notional earnings component for an employee (s 19A)?
GIVEN `the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall for this employee and the QE day, in dollars?
      `the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall for this employee and the QE day, in dollars?
      `the latest day a contribution could be applied for the QE day` IS A DATE @desc What was the latest day an eligible contribution was able to be applied for the QE day?
      `the day the assessment is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the assessment made?
      `the general interest charge rate for each day of the late period, in order` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What was the general interest charge rate for each day of the late period, as a fraction of 1 (for example 0.01 for one per cent), one after another?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my individual notional earnings component` MEANS
    `the individual notional earnings component`
        `the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall`
        `the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall`
        (`the number of days in the late period` `the latest day a contribution could be applied for the QE day` `the day the assessment is made`)
        `the general interest charge rate for each day of the late period, in order`

-- s 19B. The administrative uplift amount: 60% of the total final shortfalls and notional earnings components, reduced by an amount under the regulations.
@export What is the administrative uplift amount for the QE day (s 19B)?
GIVEN `the total of my employees' individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for the QE day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for all your employees for the QE day, in dollars?
      `the total of my employees' individual notional earnings components for the QE day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the individual notional earnings components for all your employees for the QE day, in dollars?
      `the reduction the regulations allow` IS A NUMBER @desc What reduction do the regulations allow, in dollars? (Enter 0 if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my administrative uplift amount` MEANS
    `the administrative uplift amount`
        `the total of my employees' individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for the QE day`
        `the total of my employees' individual notional earnings components for the QE day`
        `the reduction the regulations allow`

§ `Part 3: the choice loading and the total shortfall (ss 16B, 20 to 20D)`

-- s 20A to 20D. The choice loading: 25% of the contributions not made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements, up to a limit of $1,200 reduced by 25% of earlier such contributions in the notice period.
@export What is the choice loading for an employee and the QE day (ss 20 to 20D)?
GIVEN `Subdivision E applies to me for this employee and the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Subdivision E of Division 1 of Part 3 apply to you for this employee and the QE day?
      `section 20A(2) or (3) applies to some or all of my contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 20A(2) or (3) apply to some or all of your contributions for this employee and the QE day?
      `the total of my contributions to which section 20A(2) or (3) applies` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of those contributions, in dollars?
      `the sum of my other eligible contributions within the notice period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum of your other eligible contributions for this employee, to which section 20A(2) or (3) applied for earlier QE days in the notice period that includes this QE day, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my choice loading` MEANS
    `the choice loading for the employee and the QE day`
        `Subdivision E applies to me for this employee and the QE day`
        `section 20A(2) or (3) applies to some or all of my contributions`
        `the total of my contributions to which section 20A(2) or (3) applies`
        (`the choice loading limit for the QE day` `the sum of my other eligible contributions within the notice period`)

-- s 16B. The superannuation guarantee shortfall of an employer for a QE day: the sum of the base shortfalls and the choice loadings (or the final shortfalls and notional earnings components) plus the administrative uplift amount.
@export What is my superannuation guarantee shortfall for the QE day (s 16B)?
GIVEN `my employees' individual base superannuation guarantee shortfalls for the QE day` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is each employee's individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall for the QE day, in dollars?
      `my employees' choice loadings for the QE day` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is each employee's choice loading for the QE day, in dollars?
      `my employees' individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for the QE day` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is each employee's individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall for the QE day, in dollars?
      `my employees' individual notional earnings components for the QE day` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is each employee's individual notional earnings component for the QE day, in dollars?
      `my administrative uplift amount for the QE day` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your administrative uplift amount for the QE day, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my superannuation guarantee shortfall` MEANS
    `the superannuation guarantee shortfall of an employer for a QE day`
        `my employees' individual base superannuation guarantee shortfalls for the QE day`
        `my employees' choice loadings for the QE day`
        `my employees' individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for the QE day`
        `my employees' individual notional earnings components for the QE day`
        `my administrative uplift amount for the QE day`

-- s 30. Where an arrangement is made to avoid charge, the charge is the amount the Commissioner thinks would have been payable without it.
@export How much superannuation guarantee charge am I liable to pay where I made an arrangement to avoid it (s 30)?
GIVEN `I made an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an arrangement?
      `as a result my superannuation guarantee shortfall for a QE day is reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of the arrangement, is your superannuation guarantee shortfall for a QE day reduced?
      `in the Commissioner's opinion the arrangement was made solely or principally to avoid payment of the charge otherwise than in accordance with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Commissioner's opinion, was the arrangement made solely or principally for the purpose of avoiding payment of superannuation guarantee charge otherwise than in accordance with the Act?
      `the amount I would, in the Commissioner's opinion, have been liable to pay had the arrangement not been made` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount would you, in the Commissioner's opinion, have been liable to pay had the arrangement not been made, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much charge am I liable to pay under section 30` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the employer is liable under section 30`
                 `I made an arrangement`
                 `as a result my superannuation guarantee shortfall for a QE day is reduced`
                 `in the Commissioner's opinion the arrangement was made solely or principally to avoid payment of the charge otherwise than in accordance with the Act`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST liable THEN
        `the amount of superannuation guarantee charge payable under section 30`
            liable
            `the amount I would, in the Commissioner's opinion, have been liable to pay had the arrangement not been made`

§ `Part 3A: the choice of fund requirements (ss 32C to 32ZAB)`

-- s 32C(1), 32CA. A contribution to the fund the employee has chosen.
@export Is my contribution to the fund the employee chose made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements (ss 32C(1), 32CA)?
GIVEN `the fund is a chosen fund for the employee when I make the contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fund a chosen fund for the employee at the time you make the contribution?
      `the fund is an unfunded public sector scheme at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fund an unfunded public sector scheme at that time?
      `the employee is a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the Commonwealth Superannuation Scheme or the Public Sector Superannuation Scheme?
      `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you impose a direct cost or charge on the employee as a consequence of your having to contribute to that fund?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my contribution to the chosen fund compliant` MEANS
    `the contribution is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements`
        (`limb 32C(1) is met`
            `the fund is a chosen fund for the employee when I make the contribution`
            `the fund is an unfunded public sector scheme at that time`
            `the employee is a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS`)
        `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund`

-- s 32C(1A), 32CA. A contribution to the stapled fund where there is no chosen fund.
@export Is my contribution to the employee's stapled fund made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements (ss 32C(1A), 32CA)?
GIVEN `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no chosen fund for the employee at the time you make the contribution?
      `the Commissioner's most recent notification is that the fund is the stapled fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the most recent notification from the Commissioner, about a request to identify any stapled fund for the employee, that the Commissioner is satisfied the fund is the stapled fund?
      `I am required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required under section 32N to give the employee a standard choice form?
      `I have not given the form by the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not given it by the time specified?
      `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you impose a direct cost or charge on the employee as a consequence of your having to contribute to that fund?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my contribution to the stapled fund compliant` MEANS
    `the contribution is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements`
        (`limb 32C(1A) is met`
            `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time`
            `the Commissioner's most recent notification is that the fund is the stapled fund`
            `I am required under section 32N to give a standard choice form`
            `I have not given the form by the time specified`)
        `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund`

-- s 32C(2), 32CA. A contribution to a fund the employer specifies in the standard choice form where there is no chosen fund and no stapled fund.
@export Is my contribution to the fund I named on the standard choice form made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements (ss 32C(2), 32CA)?
GIVEN `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no chosen fund for the employee at the time you make the contribution?
      `the Commissioner's most recent notification is that there is no stapled fund for the employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the most recent notification from the Commissioner that the Commissioner is satisfied there is no stapled fund for the employee?
      `the fund is an eligible choice fund for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fund an eligible choice fund for you?
      `the fund is or will be specified in the standard choice form as the fund I will contribute to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fund, or will it within the time allowed be, specified under section 32P in the standard choice form as the fund you will contribute to?
      `the employee holds a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the employee hold a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958?
      `a class of beneficial interest in the fund is a MySuper product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a class of beneficial interest in the fund a MySuper product?
      `the fund complies with the regulations about death benefits for MySuper members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the fund comply with the regulations about death benefits for MySuper members?
      `the fund complies with the regulations about offering death benefits for other members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the fund comply with the regulations about offering death benefits for other members?
      `I am required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required under section 32N to give the employee a standard choice form?
      `I have not given the form by the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not given it by the time specified?
      `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you impose a direct cost or charge on the employee as a consequence of your having to contribute to that fund?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my contribution to the fund I named compliant` MEANS
    `the contribution is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements`
        (`limb 32C(2) is met`
            `there is no chosen fund for the employee at the time`
            `the Commissioner's most recent notification is that there is no stapled fund for the employee`
            `the fund is an eligible choice fund for me`
            `the fund is or will be specified in the standard choice form as the fund I will contribute to`
            `the employee holds a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958`
            `a class of beneficial interest in the fund is a MySuper product`
            `the fund complies with the regulations about death benefits for MySuper members`
            `the fund complies with the regulations about offering death benefits for other members`
            `I am required under section 32N to give a standard choice form`
            `I have not given the form by the time specified`)
        `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund`

-- s 32C(2AB), 32CA. A contribution to a new fund after a transfer without the employee's consent.
@export Is my contribution to a successor fund made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements (ss 32C(2AB), 32CA)?
GIVEN `the interest of the employee in the new fund was transferred from the original fund without the employee's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employee's interest in the new fund transferred from the original fund without the employee's consent?
      `at the time of my most recent earlier contribution to the original fund, it was a fund to which section 32C(2)(ba)(i), 32C(2)(ba)(ii) or 32C(1A) applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of your most recent earlier contribution to the original fund, was it a fund to which paragraph 32C(2)(ba)(i) or (ii) or subsection 32C(1A) applied?
      `the new fund is a successor fund in relation to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new fund a successor fund, within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997, in relation to the transfer?
      `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you impose a direct cost or charge on the employee as a consequence of your having to contribute to that fund?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my contribution to the successor fund compliant` MEANS
    `the contribution is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements`
        (`limb 32C(2AB) is met`
            `the interest of the employee in the new fund was transferred from the original fund without the employee's consent`
            `at the time of my most recent earlier contribution to the original fund, it was a fund to which section 32C(2)(ba)(i), 32C(2)(ba)(ii) or 32C(1A) applied`
            `the new fund is a successor fund in relation to the transfer`)
        `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund`

-- s 32C(6), 32CA. A contribution made under an industrial instrument.
@export Is my contribution made under an industrial agreement or award in compliance with the choice of fund requirements (ss 32C(6), 32CA)?
GIVEN `the contribution is made under a pre-reform certified agreement, an AWA, a pre-reform AWA, a collective agreement, an old IR agreement, an ITEA or an award mentioned in section 32C(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making the contribution under a pre-reform certified agreement, an AWA, a pre-reform AWA, a collective agreement, an old IR agreement, an ITEA or an award mentioned in section 32C(6)?
      `the contribution is made under a workplace determination or enterprise agreement made before 1 January 2021` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making the contribution under a workplace determination or an enterprise agreement made before 1 January 2021?
      `the Commissioner's most recent notification is that there is no stapled fund for the employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the most recent notification from the Commissioner that the Commissioner is satisfied there is no stapled fund for the employee?
      `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you impose a direct cost or charge on the employee as a consequence of your having to contribute to that fund?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my contribution under an industrial instrument compliant` MEANS
    `the contribution is made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements`
        (`limb 32C(6) is met`
            `the contribution is made under a pre-reform certified agreement, an AWA, a pre-reform AWA, a collective agreement, an old IR agreement, an ITEA or an award mentioned in section 32C(6)`
            `the contribution is made under a workplace determination or enterprise agreement made before 1 January 2021`
            `the Commissioner's most recent notification is that there is no stapled fund for the employee`)
        `I impose a direct cost or charge on the employee because of having to contribute to that fund`

-- s 32N, 32NA. Must I give this employee a standard choice form?
@export Must I give this employee a standard choice form (ss 32N, 32NA)?
GIVEN `a trigger in section 32N has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of the events in section 32N occurred (the employee was employed on 1 July 2005, started employment with you, asked you in writing for a form, or you became aware that there is no chosen fund or that you cannot contribute to the employer fund)?
      `the employee has chosen a fund under section 32F by the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the employee chosen a fund under section 32F by the time specified in section 32NA?
      `I make contributions of a kind in 32C(3) to (9) in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make contributions of a kind described in subsections 32C(3) to (9), in compliance with the choice of fund requirements?
      `the employee chose a fund before 1 July 2005 that is taken to be the chosen fund under 32F(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee choose a fund before 1 July 2005 that is taken to be the chosen fund under subsection 32F(1A), so that subsections 32N(3) and (4) do not apply?
      `the employee is a member of an unfunded public sector scheme and not a Commonwealth employee in the CSS or the PSS` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee a member of an unfunded public sector scheme, and not a Commonwealth employee who is a member of the CSS or the PSS?
      `the employee ceases to be an employee before the end of the period for giving the form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the employee cease to be an employee before the end of the period for giving the form?
      `it is a condition of employment that the employee choose from all eligible choice funds and I have no arrangement to pay to a default fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a condition of employment that the employee choose from all eligible choice funds, and do you have no arrangement to pay to a default fund?
      `the employee is a defined benefit member and subsection 20B(2) applies for the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee a defined benefit member for whom subsection 20B(2) applies for the QE day?
      `the employee is a defined benefit member and subsection 20B(3) applies for the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee a defined benefit member for whom subsection 20B(3) applies for the QE day?
      `the employee is a defined benefit member and would get the same benefit whether or not contributions are made to another fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee a defined benefit member who would be entitled to the same benefit whether or not contributions are made to another fund?
      `the employee is covered by a notional agreement preserving State awards or a preserved State agreement and I gave the State law notification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee covered by a notional agreement preserving State awards or a preserved State agreement, and did you give the State law notification?
      `the employee holds a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the employee hold a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I give this employee a standard choice form` MEANS
    `the employer must give a standard choice form`
        `a trigger in section 32N has occurred`
        (`the employer is not required under section 32N to give a standard choice form` exceptions)
    WHERE
        exceptions MEANS `Exceptions under section 32NA` OF
                                `the employee has chosen a fund under section 32F by the time specified`,
                                `I make contributions of a kind in 32C(3) to (9) in compliance with the choice of fund requirements`,
                                `the employee chose a fund before 1 July 2005 that is taken to be the chosen fund under 32F(1A)`,
                                `the employee is a member of an unfunded public sector scheme and not a Commonwealth employee in the CSS or the PSS`,
                                `the employee ceases to be an employee before the end of the period for giving the form`,
                                `it is a condition of employment that the employee choose from all eligible choice funds and I have no arrangement to pay to a default fund`,
                                `the employee is a defined benefit member and subsection 20B(2) applies for the QE day`,
                                `the employee is a defined benefit member and subsection 20B(3) applies for the QE day`,
                                `the employee is a defined benefit member and would get the same benefit whether or not contributions are made to another fund`,
                                `the employee is covered by a notional agreement preserving State awards or a preserved State agreement and I gave the State law notification`,
                                `the employee holds a temporary visa within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958`

-- s 32N. Did I give the standard choice form in time?
@export Did I give the standard choice form in time (s 32N)?
GIVEN `the event that required me to give the form` IS A `Trigger for a standard choice form` @desc Which event required you to give the standard choice form?
      `the day that event happened` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that event happen?
      `the day I gave the form` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give the employee the form?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did I give the standard choice form in time` MEANS
    `a standard choice form is given in time`
        `the event that required me to give the form`
        `the day that event happened`
        `the day I gave the form`

-- s 32P. Is my form a standard choice form?
@export Is the form I gave the employee a standard choice form (s 32P)?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form in writing?
      `it states that the employee may choose any eligible choice fund for me as a chosen fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the employee may choose any eligible choice fund for you as a chosen fund?
      `it gives the name of the fund I will contribute to if the employee does not make a choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the name of the fund you will contribute to if the employee does not make a choice?
      `it contains other information required under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the other information required under the regulations?
      `the employee is a member of a defined benefits scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee a member of a defined benefits scheme?
      `it contains the information about that scheme required under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the information about that scheme required under the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my form a standard choice form` MEANS
    `is a standard choice form`
        `it is in writing`
        `it states that the employee may choose any eligible choice fund for me as a chosen fund`
        `it gives the name of the fund I will contribute to if the employee does not make a choice`
        `it contains other information required under the regulations`
        `the employee is a member of a defined benefits scheme`
        `it contains the information about that scheme required under the regulations`

-- s 32F. From what day is the fund the employee chose a chosen fund?
@export From what day is the fund the employee chose a chosen fund for my employee (s 32F)?
GIVEN `the day the employee's notice choosing the fund is given to me` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the employee give you the notice choosing the fund?
      `the earlier time I determine` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc Did you determine an earlier day from which the fund is to be the chosen fund? If so, what day?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`From what day is the chosen fund the chosen fund` MEANS
    `the day a fund becomes a chosen fund` `the day the employee's notice choosing the fund is given to me` `the earlier time I determine`

§ `Part 4: statements and assessments (ss 33, 36, 37)`

-- s 33(2). A statement is a voluntary disclosure statement if it is lodged before the assessment day and in the approved form.
@export Is my statement a voluntary disclosure statement (s 33)?
GIVEN `the day I lodged the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lodge the statement?
      `the day an assessment is made for me for the QE day` IS A DATE @desc On what day is an assessment made for you for the QE day?
      `the statement is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement in the approved form?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my statement a voluntary disclosure statement` MEANS
    `a statement is a voluntary disclosure statement`
        `the day I lodged the statement`
        `the day an assessment is made for me for the QE day`
        `the statement is in the approved form`

-- s 36(3). If I give only a payment day, the receipt day is taken to be the seventh business day after it.
@export What receipt day is taken for a contribution if my statement gives only the payment day (s 36(3))?
GIVEN `the payment day I gave` IS A DATE @desc What payment day did you give in the statement?
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days after the payment day are public holidays?
GIVETH A DATE
`What receipt day is taken` MEANS
    `the receipt day taken where the statement gives only a payment day` `the payment day I gave` `the public holidays`

-- s 37(2). Can the Commissioner still amend my assessment to correct an avoidance of charge?
@export Can the Commissioner still amend my assessment to correct an avoidance of charge (s 37(2))?
GIVEN `there has been an avoidance of superannuation guarantee charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been an avoidance of superannuation guarantee charge?
      `the Commissioner is of the opinion that the avoidance is due to fraud or evasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commissioner of the opinion that the avoidance is due to fraud or evasion?
      `the day of the amendment` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the assessment amended?
      `the day the assessment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the assessment made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Commissioner still amend my assessment` MEANS
    `the Commissioner may amend the assessment to correct an avoidance`
        `there has been an avoidance of superannuation guarantee charge`
        `the Commissioner is of the opinion that the avoidance is due to fraud or evasion`
        `the day of the amendment`
        `the day the assessment was made`

§ `Part 6: unpaid charge (s 49)`

-- s 49. General interest charge for each day from the day the charge was due to the last day on which any of it remains unpaid at the end of the day.
@export How much general interest charge do I owe on unpaid charge (s 49)?
GIVEN `the day the charge was due to be paid` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the charge due to be paid?
      `the last day on which any of it remains unpaid at the end of the day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which, at the end of the day, any of the charge remains unpaid?
      `the general interest charge for each day in the period` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What is the general interest charge for each day in that period, in dollars, one after another?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much general interest charge do I owe` MEANS
    `the general interest charge payable under section 49`
        `the day the charge was due to be paid`
        `the last day on which any of it remains unpaid at the end of the day`
        `the general interest charge for each day in the period`

§ `Part 7: the notice to pay and the administrative penalty (ss 59A to 59E)`

-- s 59A(1). The current notice trigger day: the day after the 28-day period starting on the imposition day.
@export On what day does the current notice trigger day fall (s 59A)?
GIVEN `the imposition day` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the charge imposed?
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day does the notice trigger day fall` MEANS
    `the current notice trigger day` `the imposition day`

-- s 59A(2), (3). When must the Commissioner give me a notice to pay?
@export Must the Commissioner give me a written notice to pay the charge (s 59A)?
GIVEN `the imposition day` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the charge imposed?
      `at least some of the specified amount is the amount unpaid on the trigger day under section 59A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is at least some of the amount to be specified in the notice charge that was imposed on the imposition day and unpaid on the current notice trigger day?
      `the remainder of the specified amount is other charge of mine that is unpaid on the trigger day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the rest of the amount, if any, other charge payable by you that is unpaid on the current notice trigger day?
      `the specified amount` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount to be specified in the notice, in dollars?
      `any higher amount the regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc Do the regulations prescribe a higher amount than $30 for this purpose? If so, what amount, in dollars?
      `the day I was last given an earlier notice to pay` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If the Commissioner has given you an earlier notice to pay under section 59A, on what day was it given?
      `no part of the specified amount was in any earlier notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that no part of the amount to be specified has been included in any earlier notice to pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the Commissioner give me a notice to pay` MEANS
    `the Commissioner must give the employer a written notice to pay as soon as practicable after the current notice trigger day`
        `at least some of the specified amount is the amount unpaid on the trigger day under section 59A(1)`
        `the remainder of the specified amount is other charge of mine that is unpaid on the trigger day`
        `the specified amount`
        `any higher amount the regulations prescribe`
        (`the current notice trigger day` `the imposition day`)
        `the day I was last given an earlier notice to pay`
        `no part of the specified amount was in any earlier notice`

-- s 59A(3), 59B. When does the payment period in my notice end?
@export On what day does the payment period in my notice end (ss 59A(3), 59B)?
GIVEN `the day specified in the notice` IS A DATE @desc What day does the notice specify as the start of the payment period?
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day does the payment period end` MEANS
    `the last day of the current notice payment period` `the day specified in the notice`

-- s 59C. What percentage penalty follows if I do not pay by the end of the payment period, and what is the penalty on the amount still unpaid?
@export What administrative penalty will I owe if I do not pay by the end of the payment period (s 59C)?
GIVEN `the imposition day` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the charge imposed?
      `the day specified in the notice` IS A DATE @desc What day does the notice specify as the start of the payment period?
      `the first day a determination under section 18C(4) covers me` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If a determination under section 18C(4) covers you, on what day does it begin to cover you?
      `the last day a determination under section 18C(4) covers me` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If a determination under section 18C(4) covers you, on what day does it stop covering you? (Leave blank if it has not stopped.)
      `the days I became liable for a penalty greater than nil for an earlier notice` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On what days did you become liable under section 59C(1) for a penalty greater than nil for an earlier notice?
      `the amount that remains unpaid at the end of the payment period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the amount specified in the notice remains unpaid at the end of the payment period, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What penalty will I owe` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the percentage used to work out the penalty` coveredByDetermination
                 (`an earlier penalty falls in the 24-month period` `the day specified in the notice` `the days I became liable for a penalty greater than nil for an earlier notice`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST percentage THEN JUST (`the amount of the penalty` percentage `the amount that remains unpaid at the end of the payment period`)
    WHERE
        coveredByDetermination MEANS
            CONSIDER `the first day a determination under section 18C(4) covers me`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST firstDay THEN
                `a determination covers the employer for some part of the period for item 1`
                    `the imposition day`
                    `the day specified in the notice`
                    firstDay
                    `the last day a determination under section 18C(4) covers me`

-- s 59D(3). Is the due day in my penalty notice far enough away?
@export Is the day my penalty is due at least 14 days after the notice was given (s 59D)?
GIVEN `the day the Commissioner gave me notice of the penalty assessment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commissioner give you written notice of the penalty assessment?
      `the day specified in the notice as the day the penalty is due` IS A DATE @desc What day does the notice specify as the day the penalty is due?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my penalty due at least 14 days after the notice` MEANS
    `the penalty is due for payment on the day specified in the notice`
        `the day the Commissioner gave me notice of the penalty assessment`
        `the day specified in the notice as the day the penalty is due`

§ `Part 8: payments to employees (ss 63A to 71)`

-- s 63A. Does Part 8 apply to the payment I made?
@export Is the payment I made one to which Part 8 applies (s 63A)?
GIVEN `the payment was assessed in relation to a QE day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment of superannuation guarantee charge one that was assessed in relation to a QE day?
      `the payment was general interest charge on charge assessed in relation to a QE day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment in the form of general interest charge payable under section 49 on non-payment of charge assessed in relation to a QE day?
      `the payment was made by me or for me in respect of one or more employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made by you, or on your behalf, in respect of one or more employees?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my payment one to which Part 8 applies` MEANS
    `Part 8 applies to the payment`
        `the payment was assessed in relation to a QE day`
        `the payment was general interest charge on charge assessed in relation to a QE day`
        `the payment was made by me or for me in respect of one or more employees`

§ `Part 9: the amnesty and records (ss 74, 79)`

-- s 74(1). Do I qualify for the amnesty for my shortfall for a quarter?
@export Do I qualify for the amnesty for my superannuation guarantee shortfall for a quarter (s 74)?
GIVEN `the day the Royal Assent was received by the Treasury Laws Amendment (Recovering Unpaid Superannuation) Act 2020` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Treasury Laws Amendment (Recovering Unpaid Superannuation) Act 2020 receive the Royal Assent?
      `the day I made the disclosure to the Commissioner` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you disclose the information to the Commissioner?
      `the disclosure was in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the disclosure in the approved form?
      `the information relates to the amount of my shortfall for the quarter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to the amount of your superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter?
      `the information had not been disclosed to the Commissioner before the amnesty period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the information not been disclosed to the Commissioner before the amnesty period?
      `the last day of the quarter` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the quarter?
      `the Commissioner had told me that the Commissioner is, or intends to be, looking into my compliance for the quarter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the disclosure, had the Commissioner informed you that the Commissioner is looking into, or intends to look into, your compliance with an obligation to pay the charge for the quarter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I qualify for the amnesty` MEANS
    `an employer qualifies for an amnesty for the shortfall for a quarter`
        `the day the Royal Assent was received by the Treasury Laws Amendment (Recovering Unpaid Superannuation) Act 2020`
        `the day I made the disclosure to the Commissioner`
        `the disclosure was in the approved form`
        `the information relates to the amount of my shortfall for the quarter`
        `the information had not been disclosed to the Commissioner before the amnesty period`
        `the last day of the quarter`
        `the Commissioner had told me that the Commissioner is, or intends to be, looking into my compliance for the quarter`

-- s 74(2). If I would have a shortfall without the information, I qualify only to the extent of the increase.
@export For how much of my shortfall do I qualify for the amnesty (s 74(2))?
GIVEN `my shortfall for the quarter taking the information into account` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter taking the information into account, in dollars?
      `my shortfall for the quarter without the information` IS A NUMBER @desc What would your superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter be without the information, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`For how much of my shortfall do I qualify for the amnesty` MEANS
    `the shortfall for which the employer qualifies for the amnesty`
        `my shortfall for the quarter taking the information into account`
        `my shortfall for the quarter without the information`

-- s 79(1) to (3). Am I keeping the records section 79 requires?
@export Am I keeping the records section 79 requires (s 79)?
GIVEN `my records record and explain all transactions and other acts I engage in or am required to engage in under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your records record and explain all transactions and other acts you engage in, or are required to engage in, under the Act?
      `my records include any documents relevant to working out whether I have a shortfall for a QE day and its amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your records include any documents relevant to working out whether you have a superannuation guarantee shortfall for a QE day, and its amount?
      `my records are in writing in English or readily convertible into it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your records kept in writing in the English language, or so as to be readily accessible and convertible into writing in the English language?
      `my records let my liability under the Act be readily ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your records kept so that your liability under the Act can be readily ascertained?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I keeping the records the Act requires` MEANS
    `the employer keeps the records section 79 requires`
        `my records record and explain all transactions and other acts I engage in or am required to engage in under the Act`
        `my records include any documents relevant to working out whether I have a shortfall for a QE day and its amount`
        `my records are in writing in English or readily convertible into it`
        `my records let my liability under the Act be readily ascertained`

-- s 79(4), (5). Must I still keep these records on this day?
@export Must I still keep these records on this day (s 79(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking whether you must still keep the records?
      `the day the records were prepared or obtained` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the records prepared or obtained?
      `the day the transactions or acts the records relate to were completed` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the transactions or acts to which the records relate completed?
      `the Commissioner has told me I need not keep them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner notified you that you need not retain the records?
      `I am a company that has gone into liquidation and been finally dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a company that has gone into liquidation and been finally dissolved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I still keep these records` MEANS
    `the employer must retain the records on the day`
        `the day I am asking about`
        `the day the records were prepared or obtained`
        `the day the transactions or acts the records relate to were completed`
        `the Commissioner has told me I need not keep them`
        `I am a company that has gone into liquidation and been finally dissolved`
